Licences: libplist, libimobiledevice-glue, libtatsu, libusbmuxd: LGPL-2.1-or-later.
libirecovery: LGPL-2.1-only (its headers say "version 2.1" with no "or later" clause).
libimobiledevice: LGPL-2.1-or-later, except tools/idevicesetlocation.c (GPL-2.0-or-later).
idevicerestore: LGPL-2.1-or-later per its source headers (its COPYING and README carry the
LGPL-3.0 text). usbmuxd: GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only. Full texts: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
and vendor/src/<component>/COPYING* in the source tree (in the Arch package:
/usr/share/licenses/t1-revive/).

To obtain the sources without this tree:
    git clone <upstream> && git -C <component> checkout <base commit>
    git -C <component> apply vendor/patches/<patch>      # or: patch -p1 < vendor/patches/<patch>
The t1-revive source tree (which contains vendor/patches/ and build.sh) is available
from the project's repository at the tag matching @VERSION@.

@SHA256_*@ placeholders are filled with `sha256sum vendor/patches/*.patch` when a release is
assembled (tools/make-toolkit.sh for the toolkit, packaging/arch/PKGBUILD for the Arch
package); @VERSION@ comes from the VERSION file.
